    "max_pixels_authority": "360*420, the cap every deployed Qwen2.5-VL entrypoint in this repository already uses (generate_c02_density_view_text_embedding_HF.py:157, predict_target_qwen.py:299, generate_vision_summary.py:69, p10_score_segments.py:147, p10c_score_segments.py:137, score_segments_mllm.py:87, role3/arbitrate_qwen.py:363 all default to it, and generate_VideoMLLM_embedding_bidir_textpool_HF.py:29 calls 151200 'the deployed max_pixels'). v7 passed NO max_pixels, so its teacher saw native-resolution frames -- unlike every other Qwen2.5-VL call in the project -- and job 13852 died allocating 110.50 GiB of fp32 vision attention on a 1080x1920 item.",
