    "no_v7_record_is_salvaged": "v7 completed 400/400 HateMM prompt records, and none of them enter a v8 bank. Applying the deployed cap changes what the teacher sees for 178/200 HateMM items too, so a mixed bank would hold some items at native resolution and some capped. Uniform teacher input across the sealed tranche is a SCIENTIFIC bar, not a seal-semantics convenience.",
    "no_scientific_semantic_changed": "selection rule, tag, suffix, count, the sealed 200+200 allowlists, prompt TEXT and its four SHA-256 values, prompt-hash rule, frame index rule, frame count, transcript normalization and cap, decoding parameters, the five-rate reliability taxonomy and every threshold are byte-identical to v7 and to the v6 freeze.",
    "CHANGE_1_tranche_cap": "small_cap_gpu_seconds 7200 -> 5222. The FIRST_TRANCHE phase ceiling is UNCHANGED at 7200s; what shrinks is this tranche's reservation, because job 13852 really spent 1978 GPU-seconds and the campaign accumulator recorded it from sacct. 1978 + 5222 = 7200 exactly. Every stage that asserted == 7200 now asserts SMALL_TRANCHE_CAP_GPU_SECONDS, including the resource_final_state schema's cap_gpu_seconds const, and a self-test proves 5222 is accepted and 5223 refused against the live ledger.",
    "CHANGE_2_teacher_input_max_pixels": "max_pixels=151200 is threaded into AutoProcessor.from_pretrained. This IS a teacher-input change and is flagged as one. It is argued as protocol-faithful matching of the deployed project-wide cap, not as a convenience constant. A fail-closed pre-merge visual-token ceiling of 4096 is checked after the processor and BEFORE model.generate, so the v7 failure mode cannot recur even if an item's geometry escapes the cap.",
    "CHANGE_3_preflight_projection_gate": "the CPU preflight now measures every one of the 400 sealed items' real pre-merge visual token count by running its frozen frames through the Qwen2.5-VL image_processor on CPU (no model, CUDA explicitly unavailable), records them per item, and projects the GPU window from measured inputs. Two states only: fits by measurement -> the namespace is published; does not fit -> HALT before the namespace exists, with the numbers.",
    "CHANGE_4_frame_packs_move_to_the_cpu_preflight": "the 400 immutable eight-frame packs are now decoded, written and hash-pinned by the CPU preflight; the GPU producer may only LOAD one and HALTs if a pack is absent. Measured cost removed from the allocation: ~0.54s per HateMM item and ~3.4s per MHC_zh item of decode plus PNG encode, plus one MHC_zh item whose decord open fails and whose pyav fallback measured 32.9s. The frame BYTES are unchanged; the pyav fallback is additionally hardened from one pass holding every frame in memory (measured 2879 frames at 1920x842) to two passes retaining only the eight requested.",
    "CARRIED_FORWARD_v7_round5_observations": "NO_SEAL_SENTINEL is now IMPORTED by the gpu_ledger module rather than redefined (the v7 round-5 reviewer's explicit instruction), and a template-tamper fixture that injects NO banned token was added, so deleting the template-equality clause inside assert_teacher_visible_containment now turns a fixture red.",
    "v7_hardenings_retained_intact": "I-1 fail-closed teacher-visible identifier containment (400 IDs x 2 forms as a batch precondition before model load, re-checked per forward); I-2 known-answer selection digest vector; I-3 allocation-anchored in-job BudgetGuard with an accounting-only breach record and exit 40; the campaign-ledger pre-ticket headroom check at three points; and the authorization-flag-before-namespace-creation gate in the GPU wrapper."
